# perl5, target native: a perl of the build host with every core module (Time::Piece for the
# openssl Makefile...), whatever the distribution of the host splits out of its perl package
### It lives in its own prefix, ${GLOBAL_TOOLCHAIN_PATH}/perl5, outside the PATH of the builds:
### the perl of the host keeps serving them (with the non core modules the host installs, such as
### XML::Parser for intltool); a recipe that needs this one puts its bin directory in front of
### the PATH of its configure and make steps (see lfs/openssl)
### Plain Configure of the perl sources: no perl-cross, no target dependencies
PKG_DEPS=
PKG_CHECK="[ x$(${GLOBAL_TOOLCHAIN_PATH}/perl5/bin/perl -e 'print $^V' 2>/dev/null || :) == xv${PKG_VER} ]"
